{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":19,"code":"PSA","name":"Psalms","testament":"OT"},"chapter":32,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"d","content":["A ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["Psalm"]}," of David, Maschil. "]},{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"PSA 32:1"},"Blessed ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is he whose"]}," transgression ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," forgiven, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["whose"]}," sin ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," covered. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 32:1"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"PSA 32:2"},"Blessed ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," the man unto whom the LORD imputeth not iniquity, and in whose spirit ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["there is"]}," no guile. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 32:2"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"PSA 32:3"},"When I kept silence, my bones waxed old through my roaring all the day long. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 32:3"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"PSA 32:4"},"For day and night thy hand was heavy upon me: my moisture is turned into the drought of summer. Selah. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 32:4"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"PSA 32:5"},"I acknowledged my sin unto thee, and mine iniquity have I not hid. I said, I will confess my transgressions unto the LORD; and thou forgavest the iniquity of my sin. Selah. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 32:5"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"PSA 32:6"},"For this shall every one that is godly pray unto thee in a time when thou mayest be found: surely in the floods of great waters they shall not come nigh unto him. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 32:6"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"PSA 32:7"},"Thou ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["art"]}," my hiding place; thou shalt preserve me from trouble; thou shalt compass me about with songs of deliverance. Selah. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 32:7"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"PSA 32:8"},"I will instruct thee and teach thee in the way which thou shalt go: I will guide thee with mine eye. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 32:8"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"PSA 32:9"},"Be ye not as the horse, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["or"]}," as the mule, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["which"]}," have no understanding: whose mouth must be held in with bit and bridle, lest they come near unto thee. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 32:9"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"PSA 32:10"},"Many sorrows ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["shall be"]}," to the wicked: but he that trusteth in the LORD, mercy shall compass him about. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 32:10"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"PSA 32:11"},"Be glad in the LORD, and rejoice, ye righteous: and shout for joy, all ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["ye that are"]}," upright in heart. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 32:11"}]}]}
